---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `
<section class="post-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="post-hero-meta">
      <a href="/blog.html" class="section-label" style="text-decoration:none">← Blog</a>
      <span class="post-date">September 16, 2026</span>
      <span class="badge">Release</span>
      <span class="badge">Runtime</span>
      <span class="badge">Embedder</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="t-h1">Traverse v0.11.0: one real runtime.wasm orchestrator</h1>
    <div class="post-byline">
      <span>By <strong>Enrico Piovesan</strong></span>
      <span>4 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="post-layout">

    <article class="post-prose">

      <p><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">Traverse v0.11.0</a> is a minor lockstep crate + npm cut. The throughline is simple: native hosts and the browser embedder all drive the <em>same</em> nested-wasmi capability executor inside an application-owned <code>runtime.wasm</code>.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        Short version: one real <code>runtime.wasm</code> orchestrator across hosts. The browser no longer reimplements WASI / <code>emit_event</code> in TypeScript. Bundles must ship <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> (+ digest) or <code>BundleEmbedder.init</code> fails closed.
      </div>

      <h2 id="why">Why this cut exists</h2>

      <p>Before v0.11.0, native hosts could lean on a canned WAT fixture for the bridge, and the browser embedder had its own TypeScript WASI / <code>emit_event</code> path. Same ABI on paper; two executors in practice. Spec <code>1402-runtime-wasm-orchestrator-convergence</code> closes that gap so capability execution converges on one artifact.</p>

      <p>PR #1427 made the cut a minor on purpose: bundles without <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> (+ <code>.sha256</code>) fail at init. That is not a silent fallback.</p>

      <h2 id="native">What native gets</h2>

      <p><code>traverse-runtime-wasm</code> hosts the nested-wasmi executor. Shared, engine-agnostic <code>emit_event</code> validation and placement constraint evaluation live in <code>traverse-contracts</code>, so Wasmtime (native) and nested wasmi share one core. <code>RuntimeWasmHost</code> loads, dispatches, and drains lifecycle / domain envelopes from <code>runtime.wasm</code>; EventBroker durability stays host-owned.</p>

      <p>Swift/wasmi, Kotlin/Chicory, and .NET/Wasmtime pass the existing bridge conformance corpus against the real artifact. The digest is published through <code>runtime/native-runtime-registry.json</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="browser">What the browser gets</h2>

      <p><code>traverse-embedder-web</code> <code>BundleEmbedder</code> and <code>composedWorkflow</code> load digest-verified <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> from the app bundle and drive the same <code>runtime-wasm-bridge/1.0.0</code> ABI as native. Interim TypeScript <code>wasi.ts</code> / <code>emitEventHost.ts</code> and per-capability Host ABI import gating are gone. Starter and fixture bundles ship the artifact + digest.</p>

      <h2 id="upgrade">Upgrade notes</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Breaking (web):</strong> add <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> and <code>runtime/runtime.wasm.sha256</code> (<code>sha256:&lt;64 hex&gt;</code>) to every app bundle.</li>
        <li>Rust crate APIs for existing local Wasmtime callers are unchanged.</li>
        <li>Native host adapters keep the same bridge export surface; they must resolve the new certified digest via the native runtime artifact registry.</li>
        <li>Pin <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.11.0</code> with crates at <code>0.11.0</code> — versions are lockstep. If you consume <code>traverse-registry</code> directly, pin <code>=0.21.0</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Full notes: <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">GitHub Release</a> · <a href="/changelog.html">site changelog</a> · Announcement <a href="https://github.com/orgs/traverse-framework/discussions/1439">#1439</a>.</p>

    </article>

    <aside class="post-sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">In this post</div>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li><a href="#why">Why this cut exists</a></li>
          <li><a href="#native">What native gets</a></li>
          <li><a href="#browser">What the browser gets</a></li>
          <li><a href="#upgrade">Upgrade notes</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">Related</div>
        <ul class="related-list">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">v0.11.0 release →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/traverse-0-10-2-verified-registry-mcp.html">Traverse v0.10.2: prepare once →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/what-discover-proves.html">What /discover proves →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/discover.html">Try /discover →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</div>
`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title={"Traverse v0.11.0: one real runtime.wasm orchestrator — Traverse Blog"}
  description={"v0.11.0 converges native and browser hosts onto one nested-wasmi runtime.wasm orchestrator. Bundles must ship the artifact + digest."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/blog/traverse-0-11-0-runtime-wasm-orchestrator.html"}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Blog", href: "/blog.html" }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">.post-hero-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-hero h1 { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .post-byline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-byline strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
    .post-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px; gap: 4rem; padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .post-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; } .post-sidebar { order: -1; } }
    .post-prose { min-width: 0; }
    .post-prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.25rem 0 0.85rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
    .post-prose p, .post-prose li { color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.75; }
    .post-prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .post-prose ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .post-prose li { margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    .post-prose a { color: var(--accent); }
    .callout { background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1rem 1.15rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.65; }
    .post-sidebar { position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
    .sidebar-card { background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .sidebar-title { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
    .toc-list, .related-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .toc-list li, .related-list li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
    .toc-list a, .related-list a { color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .toc-list a:hover, .related-list a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
</SubpageLayout>
